  "headline_sentence": "Applied unchanged to 118,645 CheXpert Plus frontal studies with self-reported race (10,144 BLACK_OR_AA, 108,501 WHITE; target share 8.5%), the pr=0.75 MIMIC-installed backdoor produced a true-label transfer effect of +0.080 (SD 0.011) at the Youden's-J operating point, against a predicted-tercile estimate of +0.042; the proxy-on-true slope here is 0.53, extending the prevalence-dependent relationship measured within MIMIC (1.44 at a 45% target share, 0.68 at 21%) to an 8.5% share and confirming that the tercile proxy understates the transfer effect increasingly as the target subgroup falls below the tercile fraction."
